eady built from the total extension needed:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Remaining distance} = 450 - 200 = 250 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of miles still needing to be added to the highway to finish extending it is \\( \\boxed{250} \\).", "To solve this problem, we need to determine how many drums of paint the paint mixer can produce in one day and then use that information to find out how many days it will take to produce 360 drums of paint.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the number of drums produced per day.\nThe paint mixer produces 18 drums in 3 days. Therefore, the number of drums produced per day is:\n\\[ \\text{Drums per day} = \\frac{\\text{Total drums}}{\\text{Number of days}} = \\frac{18}{3} = 6 \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine the number of days required to produce 360 drums.\nNow that we know the paint mixer produces 6 drums per day, we can calculate the number of days needed to produce 360 drums:\n\\[ \\text{Days required} = \\frac{\\text{Total drums}}{\\text{Drums per day}} = \\frac{360}{6} = 60 \\]\n\nTherefore, it will take the paint mixer 60 days to make 360 drums of paint.\n\n#### 60", "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the total amount saved by both partners over 4 months and then determine how much they have after investing half of it in stocks.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the weekly savings for the wife.\nThe wife saves $100 per week. There are approximately 4 weeks in a month (considering a typical month has about 4 weeks).\n\nWeekly savings = $100/week * 4 weeks/month = $400/month\n\nStep 2: Calculate the monthly savings for the wife.\nMonthly savings = Weekly savings * Number of weeks in a month\n                = $400/month * 4 weeks/month = $1600/month\n\nStep 3: Calculate the total savings for the wife over 4 months.\nTotal savings for the wife = Monthly savings * Number of months\n                          = $1600/month * 4 months = $6400\n\nStep 4: Calculate the monthly savings for the husband.\nThe husband saves $225 every month.\n\nStep 5: 