nkles than eyes:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of wrinkles} = 3 \\times \\text{Number of eyes}\n   \\]\n   Given that the lizard has 3 eyes:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of wrinkles} = 3 \\times 3 = 9\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of spots:**\n   Since the lizard has 7 times more spots than wrinkles:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of spots} = 7 \\times \\text{Number of wrinkles}\n   \\]\n   We already calculated that there are 9 wrinkles:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of spots} = 7 \\times 9 = 63\n   \\]\n\n4. **Find the total number of spots and wrinkles:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total spots and wrinkles} = \\text{Number of spots} + \\text{Number of wrinkles}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the values we found:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total spots and wrinkles} = 63 + 9 = 72\n   \\]\n\n5. **Determine how many fewer eyes the lizard has compared to the combined number of spots and wrinkles:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Fewer eyes} = \\text{Total spots and wrinkles} - \\text{Number of eyes}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the known values:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Fewer eyes} = 72 -", "To find the total amount of water leaked from all three holes over a 2-hour time period, we need to calculate the leakage rate for each hole and then sum them up.\n\n1. **Largest Hole:**\n   - Leaks at a rate of 3 ounces per minute.\n   - Over 2 hours (which is 120 minutes), the total leakage would be:\n     \\[\n     3 \\text{ ounces/minute} \\times 120 \\text{ minutes} = 360 \\text{ ounces}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Medium-Sized Hole:**\n   - Leaks at half the rate of the largest hole.\n   - Therefore, its rate is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{3}{2} \\text{ ounces/minute} = 1.5 \\text{ ounces/minute}\n     \\]\n   - Over 2 hours, the total leakage would be:\n     \\[\n     1.5 \\text{ ounces/minute} \\times 120 \\text{ minutes} = 180 \\text{ ounces}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Smallest Hole:**\n   - Leaks at one-third the rate of the medium-sized hole.\n   - Therefore, its rate is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{1.5}{3} \\text{ ounces/minute} = 0.5 \\text{ ounce