l plates, there were 64 plates in the tower.\n\nNext, we know that the tower fell at 83 plates. To find out how many more plates Alice could have added before the fall, we subtract the number of plates already in the tower from the total number of plates:\n\\[ \\text{Plates left to add} = 83 - 64 \\]\n\nPerforming the subtraction:\n\\[ 83 - 64 = 19 \\]\n\nTherefore, Alice was able to add 19 more plates before the tower fell and crashed.\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{19}\n\\]", "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the area of the street.\n- The street is square-shaped with each side measuring 100 meters.\n- Area of a square = Side \u00d7 Side\n\n\\[ \\text{Area of the street} = 100 \\times 100 = 10000 \\text{ square meters} \\]\n\n### Step 2: Determine the area of the forest.\n- According to the problem, the area of the forest is three times the area of the street.\n\n\\[ \\text{Area of the forest} = 3 \\times \\text{Area of the street} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Area of the forest} = 3 \\times 10000 = 30000 \\text{ square meters} \\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the total number of trees in the forest.\n- We know that there are 4 trees per square meter in the forest.\n\n\\[ \\text{Total number of trees} = \\text{Area of the forest} \\times \\text{Trees per square meter} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total number of trees} = 30000 \\times 4 = 120000 \\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{120000}\n\\]", "To find out how many balls of wool Enid and Aaron used in total, we need to calculate the number of balls each person used separately and then add those numbers together.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the number of balls of wool Aaron used:\n- Aaron made 10 scarves.\n- Each scarf uses 3 balls of wool.\nSo, Aaron used \\(10 \\times 3 = 30\\) balls of wool on scarves.\n\nNext, let's calculate the number of balls of wool Aaron used for sweaters:\n- Aaron made 5 sweaters.\n- Each sweater uses 4 balls of wool.\nSo, Aaron used \\(5 \\times 4 = 20\\) balls of 