as 2 legs.\n   - There are 3 birds, so they have \\(3 \\times 2 = 6\\) legs.\n\n2. Dogs: Each dog has 4 legs.\n   - There are 5 dogs, so they have \\(5 \\times 4 = 20\\) legs.\n\n3. Snakes: Each snake has 0 legs (since snakes do not have limbs).\n   - There are 4 snakes, so they have \\(4 \\times 0 = 0\\) legs.\n\n4. Spider: A spider has 8 legs.\n   - There is 1 spider, so it has \\(1 \\times 8 = 8\\) legs.\n\nNow, let's add up all the legs:\n\n- Total legs from birds: 6\n- Total legs from dogs: 20\n- Total legs from snakes: 0\n- Total legs from spiders: 8\n\nTotal legs = \\(6 + 20 + 0 + 8 = 34\\)\n\nTherefore, the total number of legs at the pet shop is **34**.", "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the total cost of Jane's purchases and then subtract that from the amount she paid.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the cost of the skirts.\nJane bought 2 skirts at $13 each.\nCost of skirts = 2 * $13 = $26\n\nStep 2: Calculate the cost of the blouses.\nJane bought 3 blouses at $6 each.\nCost of blouses = 3 * $6 = $18\n\nStep 3: Calculate the total cost of all items.\nTotal cost = Cost of skirts + Cost of blouses\nTotal cost = $26 + $18 = $44\n\nStep 4: Subtract the total cost from the amount Jane paid.\nAmount paid = $100\nChange received = Amount paid - Total cost\nChange received = $100 - $44 = $56\n\nTherefore, Jane received $56 in change.\n\n#### 56", "To solve this problem, we first need to determine how many months the pasture will last without any feed corn being purchased. We know that:\n\n- Each cow eats 2 acres of grass per month.\n- Each sheep eats 1 acre of grass per month.\n\nLet's denote:\n- \\( C \\) as the number of cows,\n- \\( S \\) as the number of sheep.\n\nGiven:\n- The total number of animals is 8 (sheep) + 5 (cattle) = 13 animals.\n- There are 144 acres of grass available.\n\nWe start by calculating the total amount of grass consumed by all the animals in one month:\n\\[ \\text{Total grass consumption} = (\\text{Number of cows} \\times 2) + (\\text{