n Dew:\n\\[ \\text{Amount of Mountain Dew} = 3 \\times 3 = 9 \\text{ ounces} \\]\n\nStep 5: Confirm the total amount of the drink.\nNow, add up all the", "To find out how many miles Tom drives in a year, we need to break down the problem into two parts: the distance covered during the first 183 days and the distance covered during the remaining days of the year.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total distance covered in the first 183 days.\n- Tom rides 30 miles per day for 183 days.\n- Total distance = 30 miles/day * 183 days\n\n\\[ \\text{Total distance (first part)} = 30 \\times 183 \\]\n\nStep 2: Calculate the number of days left in the year after the first 183 days.\n- There are 365 days in a year.\n- Days left = 365 - 183\n\n\\[ \\text{Days left} = 365 - 183 \\]\n\nStep 3: Calculate the total distance covered in the remaining days of the year.\n- Tom rides 35 miles per day for the remaining days.\n- Total distance = 35 miles/day * (days left)\n\n\\[ \\text{Total distance (second part)} = 35 \\times (\\text{Days left}) \\]\n\nStep 4: Add the distances from both parts to get the total annual mileage.\n- Total annual mileage = Distance (first part) + Distance (second part)\n\n\\[ \\text{Total annual mileage} = (30 \\times 183) + (35 \\times (\\text{Days left})) \\]\n\nNow let's calculate:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total distance (first part)} = 30 \\times 183 = 5490 \\text{ miles} \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{Days left} = 365 - 183 = 182 \\text{ days", "To solve this problem, we need to determine how many pencils each person bought and then sum up their purchases.\n\n1. **Determine the number of pencils Cindi bought:**\n   - Cindi spent $30 on $0.50 pencils.\n   - Number of pencils Cindi bought = Total amount / Price per pencil\n   - Number of pencils Cindi bought = $30 / $0.50 = 60 pencils\n\n2. **Determine the number of pencils Marcia bought:**\n   - Marcia bought double the number of pencils as Cindi.\n   - Number of pencils Marcia bought = 2 * Number of pencils Cindi bought\n   - Number of 